Nicholas,

Attached is the current Japan Finance procedure for supplier payments. It sets out the 14 step=
s from receipt through to settlement reconciliation.

I am concerned that the time spent entering invoices may be holding up payments in Japan. Plea=
se examine that possibility and show us where the time is actually going across the route. I w=
ould also like Neha to check how each hand-off works in practice: what has to be present befor=
e the next person can take the item, and what happens when something is returned.

Please use the current procedure as the starting point and keep its checks in view as you asse=
ss the delays.

Kenneth

